  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Bug reported by Matt Zumwalt:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Fedora isn't proffering an authentication challenge when I hit the REST API methods.  I had to point my browser at ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "http://127.0.0.1:8080/fedora"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "http://127.0.0.1:8080/fedora",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": " in order to authenticate my browser and then go back to ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "http://127.0.0.1:8080/fedora/objects/demo:5/export"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "http://127.0.0.1:8080/fedora/objects/demo:5/export",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": "  ",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "In the past, Fedora would challenge the browser whenever it attempted to perform a protected method without authenticating, and a failed authentication would return a 400 error.  What changed that it's returning a blank page now?",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
