  "description": "<p>Bug reported by Matt Zumwalt:</p>\n\n<p>Fedora isn't proffering an authentication challenge when I hit the REST API methods.  I had to point my browser at <a href=\"http://127.0.0.1:8080/fedora\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://127.0.0.1:8080/fedora</a> in order to authenticate my browser and then go back to <a href=\"http://127.0.0.1:8080/fedora/objects/demo:5/export\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://127.0.0.1:8080/fedora/objects/demo:5/export</a>  </p>\n\n<p>In the past, Fedora would challenge the browser whenever it attempted to perform a protected method without authenticating, and a failed authentication would return a 400 error.  What changed that it's returning a blank page now?</p>",
